m the major scientific satellital telescopes must be filtered and all scientific professionals viewing the resulting data must be monitored. Should anyone manage to reconstruct an adequate data-footprint using simulations, or otherwise bypass our censorship, our surveillance may indicate they are witnessing info-hazardous data, the individual is to be designated SCP 5923-A and Protocol:Cataract is to be engaged. A raid team will be deployed from the nearest Foundation site to interrupt the viewing, though response times may vary such that the target would be home at the time of the raid. The target is to be shot with a tranquilizer, any persons in the domicile are to be also shot with tranquilizers, or otherwise subdued. All materials relating to SCP 5923-A’s research are to be seized.</p> <p>The target is to be given a Class-A amnestic, any bystanders are to be given Class-B amnestics. If the bystanders were family members or roommates of the target, the following day a Foundation Agent posing as a friend will bring the family a gift basket and offer their heartfelt condolences for the 4th anniversary of the target’s death abroad.</p> <p>Historical materials relating to a trip to a foreign country where a death certificate is easy to forge are to be introduced to the target’s computer during the raid operation, in the form of .pdf files with altered download timestamps indicating fabricated plane tickets, hotel bookings, hinging on a conference that did historically occur in that country between three and four years ago. The gift basket contains chocolates *and* a case of La Croix, both laced with class C amnestics to make the Foundation Agent be forgotten. We have found that related parties will eat the chocolates 68.5% of the time, and either the chocolates and/or the La Croix in 86.5% of cases.</p> <p>It has been concluded safer to not try to re-engage the related parties in the minority case where follow-up amestics are not consumed. A death certificate is provided whenever investigated and is, essentially, a line item expense that produces legally authentic documents. Should the world change politically such that the preceding sentence is no longer true, the protocol must be adapted.</p> <p>SCP-5923&#160;A becomes non-anomalous after the application of the class A amnestic. The complete personality rewrite necessitates that the Foundation pipeline the subject, now to be known as POI-5923-x, where x is the next available integer depending on how many are in the pipeline at the given time. A randomly generated number determines the new career for the confused individual, a training and re-education program is followed, and they proceed to live fairly stable lives. It was decided by the Ethics Committee not to re-introduce these persons to a career in astronomy or physics, because of the extreme threat level posed by SCP-5923 and its potential to unleash a VK-Universe Failure event.</p> <p>On review of seized research materials, researchers must try to ascertain which was the last measurement taken, for our tracking purposes. This scanning exercise is done by a memetically-trained Class B operating under a Class O amnestic IV drip, with a henna tattoo of their instructions on both forearms, while wearing sunglasses. If they recognize a number they believe corresponds with the last recorded negative-pressure ratio, they must shout it out and glance away as fast as possible.</p> <div class="scp-image-block block-right" style="width:300px;"><img src="http://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/scp-5923/Quasars.png" style="width:300px;" alt="Quasars.png" class="image" /> <div class="scp-image-caption" style="width:300px;"> <p>Non-infohazardous examples of quasar redshift that suggested the Big Rip theory.</p> </div> </div> <p><strong>Description:</strong></p> <p>SCP-5923 is the catalyzation effect of hastening the arrival of The Big Rip by viewing a time series of measurements of distant quasar redshift, making projections from th