he stars in our galaxy or its spiral shape being kneaded into a more globular elliptical, because there would not be nearly enough time for that light to reach us.</p> <p><strong>Phase 5</strong>: Separation of The Solar System</p> <p>Worst-case, this takes about 90 to 100 minutes. Because we are 8 light-minutes away from the sun, we would not see the already orange-spectrum sunlight start to significantly red shift until we had reached an orbital distance of &gt;10 AU. In the last 10 or 20 minutes of this period the earth’s orbit would find its path out where the Oort cloud used to be. Those who have adequate shelter and energy would probably survive the first half of this period but atmospheric disturbances would begin depriving non-Foundation populations of oxygen.</p> <p><strong>Phase 6</strong>: Tidal Shearing of The Earth</p> <p>Worst-case estimate, 25 minutes.</p> <p><strong>Phase 7</strong>: Bunker Rupture</p> <p>10 minutes.</p> <p><strong>Phase 8</strong>: Holding On To Someone While Dying in The Vacuum</p> <p>3-4 minutes.</p> <p><strong>Phase 9</strong>: SCPs, O5 and below personnel with adequate gear, other GoI personnel with adequate gear, the last surviving entities, begin to be torn apart due to the repulsive phantom energy overcoming electromagnetic chemical bonds.</p> <p>90 seconds</p> <p><strong>Phase 10</strong>: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2100">SCP-2100-4</a> begins to shear apart.</p> <p><strong>Phase 11</strong>: All spacetime anomaly SCPs begin to have scalar manifold interactions with the dark energy singularity in unpredictable ways. All spatially infinite structural anomalies are unfurled, releasing energy into the void. <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-319">SCP-319's</a> restraints have been destroyed by this time, unleashing the low-energy vacuum expansion, which would interact with the Big Rip by diluting its energy density. <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2821">SCP-2821</a> may have already become unstable far sooner and 